# Prettier's ignore-file lookup is CWD-relative (unlike its `.prettierrc` config resolution,
# which searches upward) — the root `.prettierignore` alone does not reach `prettier --check .`
# run from this package's directory (`pnpm --filter @onchain-intel/mcp-server run format:check`).
# This package-local file is the minimal fix: `dist/` is tsup/tsc build output, never hand-formatted.
#
# **The asymmetry runs BOTH ways, and only one half was written down here.** Nested ignore files are
# not consulted either, so an entry that exists only in this file does NOT cover the root
# `prettier --check .` — which is the invocation CI runs (.github/workflows/ci.yml). TASK-011 added
# the two generated artifacts below to this file alone and left the branch failing CI until the
# adversarial cycle ran the root gate instead of the filtered one. Anything added here that is not
# `dist/` must be added to the root `.prettierignore` as well.
dist/
# Generated by scripts/snapshot-tools.ts (TASK-011 R-125). The generator OWNS this file's byte
# format: `test/tools-list-contract.test.ts` compares the published `tools/list` output to it
# byte for byte, and prettier re-wrapping the JSON would make that comparison fail on a tree where
# nothing about the contract changed.
test/fixtures/tools-list.snapshot.json
# Generated by scripts/gen-tool-inventory.ts (TASK-011 R-114) and compared byte for byte by
# test/tool-inventory-in-sync.test.ts. Same reason as the snapshot above: the generator owns the
